/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  postProcessDict -- THE NANOFILTRAN PAPER'S TABLES AND FIGURES, GENERATED FROM THE
  RUN (DEV.md 4c C147; Vitor: "Um pos processamento nao gera os graficos e
  tabelas que sao precisos para este artigo?").

  Every plot and table below names what the run PUBLISHES -- an operation's
  diagnostics (`ops ( ... ); x <diag>; y <diag>;`), an operation's published
  table (`op <op>; table points|pore; x <col>; y <col>;`) -- and case-local
  REFERENCE data under constant/ with its citation.  The engine refuses a
  name it cannot resolve, holds every unit the source publishes to the unit
  declared here, and writes postProcessing/postProcessDict/<name>.csv (+ <name>.json)
  on every run; the GUI's Plot workspace draws them under "Post-processing"
  and computes nothing -- a difference column is the engine's.  The grammar:
  docs/design/a-post-processing-dictionary.md.

  The NanoFiltran numbers in constant/reference/ are EXPORTED from
  bin/curate/nanofiltran/ (paper.tsv, fig4_profiles.tsv, reference.tsv) by
  bin/curate/nanofiltran/export_case.py; bin/curate/check_postprocessing.py
  holds them to that source and every cell of every output to its own.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

